          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Chern-Simons element
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebroid"} L-∞ algebroid
            (named after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shiing-shen+Chern"} Shiing-shen Chern
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"} James Simons
            who considered this for
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+algebras"} semisimple Lie algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            that exhibits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            between an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid+cocycle"} ∞-Lie algebroid cocycle
            and an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
          %p
            It is construct that arises in the presentation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} ∞-Chern-Weil homomorphism
            by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-anafunctor"} ∞-anafunctor
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We discuss
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra"} ∞-Lie algebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid"} ∞-Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            in terms of their
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            = succeed "." do
