                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\mu) : \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^n \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group+cohomology"} Lie group cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            for discussion of the refined notion of Lie group cohomology arising here.)
          %p
            The differential refinement of these construction is based on the following fact (discussed in detail
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid#StrucCurvatureForms"} here
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi n
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1) \in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
                is equivalently presented by a quotient of the presheaf of
                = succeed "es" do
