              %p and then picks out the bottom horizontal morphism.
          %p
            Therefore our task of presenting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mi dR
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}_{dR}
            amounts to computing the composition of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-anafunctor"} ∞-anafunctor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
