            any higher order cocycle,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CS
                    %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS_\mu(A)
            is the corresponding higher order Chern-Simons form.
          %h4#action_functional_for_chernsimons_supergravity Action functional for Chern-Simons (super-)gravity
          %p
            Higher Chern-Simons elements on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+Lie+algebra"} Poincare Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝔦𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} = \mathfrak{iso}(d,1)
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincare+Lie+algebra"} super Poincare Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} = \mathfrak{siso}(d,1)
            yield
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
          %p (…)
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Zanelli"}> Zanelli
            ).
          %h4#fractional_secondary_pontryagin_classes Fractional secondary Pontryagin classes
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_7
            the 7-cocycle on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+algebra"} semisimple Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CS
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS_{\mu_7}(A)
            is the corresponding Chern-Simons 7-form, corresponding to the second
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+class"} Pontryagin class
          %p
            Notice that this we may also think of as a 7-cocycle on the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-algebra"} string Lie 2-algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane+Lie+6-algebra"} fivebrane Lie 6-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+7-bundle+with+connection"} Chern-Simons circle 7-bundle with connection
            that obstructions the lift from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differential string structure
            to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+fivebrane+structure"} differential fivebrane structure
          %h3#BF On strict Lie 2-algebras – BF-theory action functional
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∂
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} = (\mathfrak{g}_2 \stackrel{\partial}{\to} \mathfrak{g})_1
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+Lie+2-algebra"} strict Lie 2-algebra
            %p Then
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi inv
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1} \in inv(\mathfrak{g}_1)
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1
                  is a Chern-Simons element on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+cocycle"} ∞-Lie algebra cocycle
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+algebra"} semisimple Lie algebra
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle - \rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                  the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+form"} Killing form
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued forms
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 2
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝔤
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝔤
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi b
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Omega^\bullet(X) \stackrel{(A,B)}{\leftarrow}
                        W(\mathfrak{g}_2 \to \mathfrak{g}_1)
                        \\stackrel{(\langle - \rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}, d_W \langle - \rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1} )}{\leftarrow}
                        W(b^{n-1} \mathbb{R})
            %p
              is the sum of the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Yang-Mills+theory"} topological Yang-Mills theory
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BF-theory"} BF-theory
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
              (in the sense of
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity+as+a+BF-theory"} gravity as a BF-theory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CS
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CS_{\langle-\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}}(A,B)
                    \=
                    \\langle F_A \wedge F_A\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                    \-
                    2\langle F_A \wedge \partial B\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                    +
                    2\langle \partial B \wedge \partial B\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_A
              is the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
              2-form of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            This is from (
            %a{:href => "#SSSI-BFtheory"}> SSSI
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{t_a\}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{b_i\}
              a basis of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_2
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mi a
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{W(\mathfrak{g})} : \sigma t^a \mapsto
                    d_{W(\mathfrak{g}_1)}
                    +
                    \\partial^a{}_i \sigma b^i
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1} = P_{a_1 \cdots a_n} \sigma r^{a_1} \wedge \cdots \sigma t^{a_n}
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{W(\mathfrak{g})} \langle - \rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                    \=
                    n P_{a_1 \cdots a_n}\partial^{a_1}{}_i  \sigma b^{i} \wedge \cdots \sigma t^{a_n}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The right hand is a polynomial in the shifted generators of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle - \rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
              is a Chern-Simons element for it.
            %p
              Now for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra-valued+form"} ∞-Lie algebra-valued form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_{(A,B)}^1 = F_A - \partial B
                    \\,.
            %p Therefore
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi CS
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi 𝔤
                                      %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %msubsup
                              %mi F
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ,
                                %mi B
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝔤
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi A
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝔤
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi A
                            %mo ∧
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi B
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝔤
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi B
                            %mo ∧
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi B
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝔤
                                  %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    CS_{\langle -\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}}(A,B)
                    \&amp; = \langle F_{(A,B)}^1\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\langle F_A \wedge F_A\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                    \-
                    2\langle F_A \wedge \partial B\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                    +
                    2\langle \partial B \wedge \partial B\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}_1}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %h3#Symplectic
            On symplectic
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{a}, \omega)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid"} Lie n-algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
            equipped with a binary non-degenerate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in W(\mathfrak{a})
            of degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+2
          %p
            The corresponding Chern-Simons elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            are the integrands for the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
          %p
            With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo :
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-,-\} : CE(\mathfrak{a}) \otimes CE(\mathfrak{a}) \to CE(\mathfrak{a})
            the graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            induced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            we have (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Roytenberg"} Roytenberg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+cocycle"} ∞-Lie algebra cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \in CE(\mathfrak{a})
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE(\mathfrak{a})} = \{\mu, -\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            So in particular
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            being a cocycle means that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi μ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE(\mathfrak{a})} \mu = \{\mu, \mu\} = 0
                  \\,.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              is in transgression with the invariant polynomial
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{n}{2}\omega
              via the Chern-Simons element
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi cs
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi ι
                              %mi ϵ
                            %mi ω
                            %mo −
                            %mi μ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    cs &amp;= \frac{1}{2 }\iota_{\epsilon} \omega - \mu
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              is the Euler vector field (
              %a{:href => "#Roytenberg"}> Roytenberg
              ).
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}
            is the shift derivation in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{W(\mathfrak{a})} = d_{CE(\mathfrak{a})} + \mathbf{d}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p To safe typing signs, we write as if all functions were even graded. By standard reasoning the computation holds true then also for arbitrary grading.
            %p Observe that
            %ol
              %li
                %p on unshifted generators we have
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo =
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (\mathbf{d}x^b) \omega_{a b} \{x^a  , -\} = \mathbf{d}
              %li
                %p we have graded commutators
                %ul
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %mi N
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbf{d}, \iota_v] = N
                    (the degree operator)
                %p and
                %ul
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mi CE
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mi CE
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [d_{CE(\mathfrak{a})}, \iota_v] = -d_{CE(\mathfrak{a})}\mathbf{d}^{-1}
                    \.
                %p (as one checks on generators).
            %p Therefore
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi W
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi 𝔞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi ι
                              %mi v
                            %mi ω
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi W
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi 𝔞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi ι
                              %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                            %mi ω
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi CE
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi 𝔞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                            %mi ω
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                            %mi ω
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi μ
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi b
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                            %mi ω
                            %mo +
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi d
                            %mi μ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    d_{W(\mathfrak{a})} \frac{1}{2}\iota_{v} \omega
                    \&amp;=
                    [d_{W(\mathfrak{a})}, \iota_{v}] \frac{1}{2}\omega
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    (n - d_{CE(\mathfrak{a})} \mathbf{d}^{-1} ) \frac{1}{2}\omega
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\frac{n}{2}\omega - \omega_{a b} \{\mu, x^a\} \mathbf{d}x^b
                    \\\
                    \&amp;= \frac{1}{2} \omega + \mathbf{d}\mu
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where in the first line we used that by definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ω
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{W(\mathfrak{a})} \omega = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{CE(\mathfrak{a})} \mu = 0
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi μ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{W(\mathfrak{a})} \mu = \mathbf{d}\mu
                    \\,.
            %p So in total we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi ω
                    %mo −
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{W(\mathfrak{a})} (\frac{1}{2} \iota_\epsilon \omega - \mu)
                    \=
                    \\frac{1}{2}\omega
                    \\,.
          .remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              In local coordinates where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega = \omega_{a b} \mathbf{d}x^a \wedge \mathbf{d}x^b
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cs
                    %mo =
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %mi μ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cs = n \omega_{a b} x^a \wedge \mathbf{d}x^b + \mu
                    \\,.
            %p
              The Chern-Simons action functional corresponding to this Chern-Simons element on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              is that considered in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+theory"} AKSZ theory
            %p Below we spell out some low-dimensional cases explicitly.
          %h4#higher_phase_space_hamiltonian_and_lagrangian_mechanics Higher phase space —Hamiltonian and Lagrangian mechanics
          %p
            The symplectic Lie
            = succeed "-algebroid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
            may be thought of as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-symplectic+manifold"} n-symplectic manifold
            that models the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of a physical system.
          %p
            This means for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔓
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g},\langle-\rangle) = (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
            a symplectic Lie
            = succeed "-algebroid," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheDiagram"} (1)
            exhibiting the transgression between cocycles and invariant polynomials via Chern-Simons elements may be labeled in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+mechanics"} Hamiltonian mechanics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+mechanics"} Lagrangian mechanics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            as follows
          #eq:PhysicsDiagram.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi CE
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔓
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mi H
                        %mtd
                          %mi CE
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
